1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,136
A coding agent writes a patch, runs its tests, and says "done". But the issue never said whether round_half(x=-12.5) is -12 or -13, and the tests never asked.

2
00:00:14,136 --> 00:00:28,176
The Behavioral Disagreement Gate asks three models for patches through Nebius Token Factory, runs them on the same inputs in isolated ConTree sandboxes, and withholds approval while any two disagree.

3
00:00:28,176 --> 00:00:44,424
A live session. Each candidate is one chat completion to Token Factory's OpenAI-compatible endpoint: NVIDIA Nemotron-3 Ultra, Qwen3, DeepSeek-V4, temperature 0.8, fixed seed per slot.

4
00:00:44,424 --> 00:00:56,976
Round 1: the candidates disagree at round_half(x=-12.5): -12 or -13. No model names, no vote counts, always "not sure".

5
00:00:56,976 --> 00:01:09,048
Before answering, one runtime call to Tavily, Nebius's search API, for the convention behind this disagreement. Sources shown, never read by the verdict.

6
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:16,656
I choose o2, -13. The answer becomes a ledger decision and an acceptance test.

7
00:01:16,656 --> 00:01:24,744
Round 2: one candidate still violates that test and is dropped by the regression gate. PASS.

8
00:01:24,744 --> 00:01:32,688
On the public site, the browser re-scores the recorded trace and prints the same decision_core hash as Python.

9
00:01:32,688 --> 00:01:40,632
The Tavily block is labelled "not read by the verdict"; in the ledger it sits between question and answer.

10
00:01:40,632 --> 00:01:50,544
Round 2 on the site: PASS, with one candidate dropped. All 84 committed runs re-score identically in the browser: 84/84.

11
00:01:50,544 --> 00:02:00,048
Same candidates, same seed, local subprocess and Nebius ConTree sandbox: three runs, one decision hash.

12
00:02:00,048 --> 00:02:08,496
If every candidate violates a past decision the same way, they agree, and the disagreement gate is silent.

13
00:02:08,496 --> 00:02:15,864
Regression gate G4 off: case A passes with three violators approved.

14
00:02:15,864 --> 00:02:21,864
G4 on: CODE_INCOMPLETE. Only the ledger catches this.

15
00:02:21,864 --> 00:02:28,176
PASS means no counterexample in the searched range; what was not searched is grey.

16
00:02:28,176 --> 00:02:38,928
The limits are stated: eight pure Python functions, live sessions on one task, a pre-alpha sandbox SDK, a search that can be wrong.

17
00:02:38,928 --> 00:02:46,536
Code, data and the demo are public. When candidates disagree, ask; never guess.
